    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d600-a1">

                <pb facs="0674" n="594" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg594"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The committee of safety to
                        Mr. Powell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: We have the honor to bring to the
                    knowledge of your excellency that there has been formed at Port au Prince a
                    committee of public safety, composed of Gens. Boisrond Canal, Horelle
                    Monplaisir, Justin Carrié Diogěne Délinois, Edmond Polynice, H. Baussan, Ney
                    Caymitte, and citizens Solon Ménos, Cadestin Robert, McDonald Appolon, and
                    Michel Oreste.</p>
                <p>This committee takes immediately and of urgence all the proper measures to assure
                    order, security, and the carrying on of all the public services.</p>
                <p>In begging your excellency to kindly take notice of this communication, we profit
                    by the occasion to assure you, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Boisrond Canal</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">President of the Committee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
